{"parse":{"title":"2026–27 UEFA Nations League A","pageid":72856417,"revid":1379947117,"redirects":[],"wikitext":"{{Use dmy dates|date=February 2026}}\n{{Infobox international football competition\n| tourney_name   = UEFA Nations League A\n| year           = 2026–27\n| dates          = ''League phase:''<br />24 September – 17 November 2026<br />''Quarter-finals:''<br />25–30 March 2027<br />''Nations League Finals:''<br />9–13 June 2027\n| num_teams      = 16\n| champion       =\n| count          =\n| second         =\n| third          =\n| fourth         =\n| relegated      =\n| matches        = 32\n| goals          = 97\n| attendance     = {{#invoke:Football attendance summation|main|groups=leaguea}}\n| top_scorer     = {{fbicon|ENG}} [[Harry Kane]]<br>(6 goals)\n| updated        = 6 October 2026\n| prevseason     = [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League A|2024–25]]\n| nextseason     = ''2028–29''\n}}\nThe '''2026–27 UEFA Nations League A''' is the top division of the [[2026–27 UEFA Nations League|2026–27 edition]] of the [[UEFA Nations League]], the fifth season of the international [[Association football|football]] competition involving the men's national teams of the member associations of [[UEFA]]. League A began with the league phase in September 2026, and will culminate with the [[2027 UEFA Nations League Finals|Nations League Finals]] in June 2027 to determine the champions of the competition.\n\n[[Portugal national football team|Portugal]] are the defending champions, having won the [[2025 UEFA Nations League Finals|2025 finals]].\n\n==Format==\nLeague A consists of the 16 top-ranked UEFA members from the [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League#Final overall ranking|2024–25 UEFA Nations League final overall ranking]], split into four groups of four. Each team will play six matches within their group, using the home-and-away [[Round-robin tournament|round-robin]] format on matchdays in September, October and November 2026.<ref name=\"need to know\">{{cite news |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefanationsleague/news/0298-1d6ef1acfaef-b54fcf1da859-1000/ |title=2026/27 UEFA Nations League: All you need to know |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=9 February 2026 |access-date=11 February 2026}}</ref>\n\nFollowing the league phase, the top two teams of each group will advance to the quarter-finals, played home-and-away over [[Two-legged tie|two legs]] in March 2027. In each tie, group winners will face a runner-up from a different group, with the group winner hosting the second leg. The four quarter-final winners will advance to the [[2027 UEFA Nations League Finals]]. The two worst last-placed teams of each group will be relegated directly to League B, while the two best last-placed teams and two worst third-placed teams will compete against the runners-up of [[2026–27 UEFA Nations League B|League B]] to either retain their place in League A for the [[2028–29 UEFA Nations League A|next season]], or face relegation to [[2028–29 UEFA Nations League B]]. The relegation play-offs will be played home-and-away over two legs in March 2027, with the League A teams hosting the second leg. In all two-legged ties, the team that scores more goals on aggregate is the winner. If the aggregate score is level, [[Overtime (sports)#Association football|extra time]] will be played without the [[away goals rule]]. If the score remains level after extra time, a [[Penalty shoot-out (association football)|penalty shoot-out]] will be used to decide the winner.<ref name=\"regulations\">{{cite web |url=https://documents.uefa.com/r/Regulations-of-the-UEFA-Nations-League-2026/27-Online |title=Regulations of the UEFA Nations League 2026/27 |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=December 2025 |access-date=13 December 2025 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260211170553/https://documents.uefa.com/api/khub/maps/HlG1NvOr4H_30IjSKzlRKg/attachments/2b1W4zSbckOh3ZMUhu0_wg-HlG1NvOr4H_30IjSKzlRKg/content |archive-date=11 February 2026}}</ref>\n\nOriginally, the format for promotion and relegation would have involved all last-placed teams in League A being relegated. The promotion/relegation play-offs would have concerned all third-placed teams in League A and all runners-up in League B. However, due to the [[UEFA Nations League#Post-2028 review and proposed format changes|changes scheduled for the 2028–29 UEFA Nations League]], in which the competition will be reduced from four leagues to three leagues of 18 teams, promotion/relegation was rebalanced to make all three upcoming leagues be at 18 teams.<ref>{{cite web |date=15 September 2026 |title=New promotion/relegation system for UEFA Nations League 2026/27 |url=https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/02a9-21985b7e3370-3f0fda209606-1000/promotion_and_relegation_unl_website.pdf |access-date=18 September 2026 |publisher=[[UEFA]]}}</ref>\n\nThe Nations League Finals will be played in a knockout format in June 2027, consisting of the semi-finals, third place play-off and final. The semi-final pairings will be determined using an open draw. The host country will be selected by the UEFA Executive Committee, preferably hosted by one of the participating teams, with the winners of the final crowned as the champions of the UEFA Nations League.<ref name=\"regulations\"/>\n\n==Teams==\nLeague A includes sixteen teams based on the results of the [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League|2024–25 season]]: the top eight teams (group winners and runners-up) from [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League A#Groups|League A]], the four winners of the [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League promotion/relegation play-offs#League A vs League B|League A/B play-offs]] and the four group winners from [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League B|League B]]. \n\n===Team changes===\nThe following were the team changes in League A from the [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League A|2024–25 season]]:<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefanationsleague/news/0292-1c2abf3ccd56-d65f5c73f690-1000/ |title=Nations League final standings: Who made the quarter-finals? Who's been promoted? Who's been relegated? Who's in the play-offs? |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=22 November 2024 |access-date=11 February 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefanationsleague/news/0296-1d165d4a3647-4d55eede66c2-1000/ |title=Nations League play-offs: Results, promotion and relegation |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=23 March 2025 |access-date=11 February 2026}}</ref>\n\n{|\n|- style=\"vertical-align:top\"\n|\n{| class=\"wikitable\" style=\"width:200px\"\n|+ Incoming\n|-\n! Promoted from<br />[[2024–25 UEFA Nations League B|Nations League B]]\n|-\n| {{Plainlist|\n* {{fb|CZE}}\n* {{fb|ENG}}\n* {{fb|GRE}}\n* {{fb|NOR}}\n* {{fb|TUR}}\n* {{fb|WAL}}\n}}\n|}\n|\n{| class=\"wikitable\" style=\"width:200px\"\n|+ Outgoing\n|-\n! Relegated to<br />[[2026–27 UEFA Nations League B|Nations League B]]\n|-\n| {{Plainlist|\n* {{fb|BIH}}\n* {{fb|HUN}}\n* {{fb|ISR}}\n* {{fb|POL}}\n* {{fb|SCO}}\n* {{fb|SUI}}\n}}\n|}\n|}\n\n===Seeding===\nThe teams were seeded for the league phase based on the [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League#Final overall ranking|2024–25 Nations League final overall ranking]], considering promotion and relegation between the leagues and the results of the [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League A#Knockout stage|League A knockout stage]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/029a-1df96111817a-2669251e926b-1000/unl_final_overall_rankings_after_unlf_2025.pdf |title=Final overall rankings of the UEFA Nations League 2024/25 (updated following the UNL finals 2025) |publisher=[[UEFA]] |access-date=24 October 2025}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |url=https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/02a1-1fc00969b028-b36e773fcfc7-1000/20260123_circular_2026_03_en.zip |title=UEFA Nations League 2026/27 – League phase draw and fixture list procedures |number=03/2026 |magazine=UEFA Circular Letter |publisher=[[UEFA]] |date=23 January 2026 |access-date=11 February 2026}}</ref>\n\n{|\n|- style=\"vertical-align:top\"\n|\n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n|-\n|+ Pot 1\n|-\n! width=\"190\" | Tea